+
+### ECON-02B2d7 — NPC construction material logistics (Linux local prototype)
+
+Construction modules now move through an authoritative, persisted supply chain:
+**colony ship -> site depot -> named worker cargo -> construction-cell delivery -> installed fixture**.
+Crews pick up and carry real modules, navigate around installed walls and doors,
+wait for deliveries before working, and return unused carried cargo after a plan
+is canceled. The colony GUI shows local stock and allows manual depot transfers.
+World snapshots track these custody transfers; work orders and NPC positions remain
+in SQLite. Tests cover cargo survival across restart and module/mass conservation.
+
+Verification: 65/65 non-live and 27/27 complementary live/relay native tests;
+93/93 JS tests; two offline Chromium colony browser tests. Windows GUI acceptance
+is open. See `docs/engineering/ECON02B2d7_NPC_Material_Logistics_Engineering_Report_2026-11-01.md`.
