@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# ECON-02B2d7 — Physical NPC construction material logistics
+
+**Date:** 2026-11-01
+**Project:** Single Galaxy (the original space-colony game; not the EvEmu educational audit)
+**Baseline:** `SingleGalaxy_ECON02B2d6_NPC_Construction_Crews_Source_Tests_2026-11-01.zip`
+**Status:** Locally implemented on Linux; regression-tested; not yet published to the GitHub source tree or accepted on Windows.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Make construction supplies physical and conserved across the colony ship, an outpost's site depot, an identified worker's carried cargo, a construction-cell delivery cache, and the installed structure. Existing NPCs, rather than generated labor tokens, perform the pickup, travel, delivery, and construction steps. Preserve the one-authoritative-writer design of ECON-02B2d4c4, physical construction rules from d5, and persisted worker identities from d6.
+
+## Implemented system
+
+1. **Canonical supply ledger in the authoritative simulation.** `ConstructionSupplies` is keyed by outpost entity ID and contains depot stock, `carried` modules keyed by actual NPC identity, and `delivered` modules keyed by construction cell. The resource is the manufactured construction module already supported by the world, not a newly minted currency. The world snapshot advances to format v32 to preserve these balances; load validation rejects malformed amounts and actions.
+2. **Four custody-transfer actions.** `StageConstructionModules` moves real modules between the colony ship and owned outpost depot, supporting positive staging and negative withdrawal. `PickupConstructionModules` transfers depot stock into eligible named NPC custody (nominal carrying limit: 2). `DeliverConstructionModules` moves the NPC's cargo into the targeted site cell. `ReturnConstructionModules` returns unspent cargo to the depot. Each goes through the simulation command/receipt path and persistence ledger.
+3. **Delivery-backed construction action.** `BuildColonyFixtureFromDelivery` uses delivered site-cell stock for an authorized existing structural plan. It does not double-charge the ship or allow construction when deliveries are absent. Existing manual building remains available as a separate, explicit action.
+4. **NPC route and work orchestration.** A worker must reach the depot (local grid origin), pick up the required quantity, walk through passable cell edges toward the plan's next fixture, deliver modules, and contribute work. The path respects installed walls and door state and uses bounded local search. The crew scheduler executes inside the primary colony simulation's command loop.
+5. **Restocking and interfaces.** The crew can stage a bounded amount from its valid source colony ship when site stock is empty; players can also stage/withdraw modules using the colony interface's depot controls. The site-specific `/factory/api/crew_supply` request uses the established token, ownership, same-origin and input-validation path; `CREW_SUPPLY` is handled by the existing native colony process, not a second world writer. The colony screen shows available depot stock, in-transit cargo, delivered stock, and per-NPC custody.
+6. **Pause, cancellation, and restart.** Crew assignment/position/labor state remains in SQLite, while physical custody is saved in the canonical world snapshot. Worker cargo survives a shutdown/restart. A canceled plan does not construct additional fixtures and worker-held unspent modules return via an explicit transfer action. A carrying worker cannot be silently unassigned and drop their cargo into a void.
+
+## Resource invariants / tests
+
+The native `ECON02B2d7_NPCMaterialHauling` test provisions a real outpost and resident NPC; creates an authorized structural plan; stages and picks up manufactured modules; verifies total world material mass; closes the world while a worker is carrying cargo; reopens SQLite; confirms the same NPC owns the module; rejects a forged pickup; completes construction from delivered stock; verifies one module moved out of active custody and into the installed structure; cancels another plan in transit; returns unspent cargo; and verifies post-cancellation and post-restart conservation. The test explicitly counts ship modules + depot + carried + delivered; it never treats the ship inventory as the entire universe's supply.
+
+The existing live colony HTTP test now exercises ship/depot transfers, ownership/session checks, malformed quantities and restart, through the real native colony process. Chromium's offline UI smoke tests exercise the new depot controls; these are mocked DOM interactions and are **not** evidence of live browser-to-localhost access. That distinction is covered independently by the host test.
+
+### Final local verification (2026-11-01)
+
+| Verification | Observed outcome |
+|---|---|
+| Full CMake native build, incremental completion | Pass |
+| CTest excluding live/relay/HTTP (`-E '(live|relay|_HTTP|_http)'`) | **65 / 65 passed** |
+| Complementary live/relay/HTTP CTest (`-R '(live|relay|_HTTP|_http)'`) | **27 / 27 passed** |
+| Combined coverage of those disjoint CTest groups | **92 / 92 passed**, not one uninterrupted run |
+| JavaScript `node --test tests/*.js` | **93 / 93 passed** |
+| `scripts/colony_crew_browser_smoke.py` | Pass (offline Chromium DOM test) |
+| `scripts/colony_structures_browser_smoke.py` | Pass (offline Chromium DOM test) |
+| Dedicated material-hauling native test | Pass (included in 65) |
+| Live colony host HTTP test | Pass (included in 27) |
+| Windows native build and GUI acceptance | **Not run / still open** |
+| Direct Chromium-to-localhost click-through in this environment | **Not established**; previously blocked by browser policy |
+
+Logs retained in the development working directory under `/mnt/data/work_b2d7/` during this task; build outputs and SQLite fixtures are intentionally excluded from the source distribution.
+
+## Security and failure model
+
+- New transfers require a legitimate owner, ship, outpost and eligible NPC. The HTTP surface uses the same authenticated, site-scoped relay as existing construction actions and checks strict numeric request shape.
+- Stock transfers are committed as authoritative commands and receipts so snapshot/restart consistency remains testable. Invalid transfer attempts must not remove ship, depot, or worker inventory.
+- A site-local outpost depot does not represent magical cross-system inventory. The colony ship source and the worker must already be eligible at that site.
+- Existing world-writer containment applies: the colony host holds the world write lease; the standalone factory runtime must not write the same SQLite world concurrently.
+- A canceled plan retains installed fixtures, and unbuilt modules stay within physical custody. The system does not reverse already completed buildings without a later dismantling feature.
+
+## Explicitly deferred
+
+- **Physical cross-colony freight**, storage-node pickup selection and vehicle-based supply runs (current material depot stages from the valid colony ship at the same site).
+- **Full 3D navigation** and rich movement around arbitrary factory geometry (this is grid/edge navigation with bounded search).
+- **NPC needs, shifts, injury and multi-step role proficiency** beyond the existing resident eligibility model.
+- **Material varieties** (current implementation uses manufactured construction modules rather than configurable per-material bill-of-materials).
+- **Delivered-stock salvage/reallocation** and priority reservations among competing plans; must design explicit accounting before automating transfers out of completed/canceled site-cell caches.
+- **Windows desktop installer/GUI acceptance** and real Chromium-to-localhost end-to-end click test in a browser environment that permits local navigation.
+
+## Next engineering gate
+
+**ECON-02B2d8 — Multi-source site logistics and allocation:** authorize supply pickup from actual storage nodes, implement demand reservations and route selection across distinct local supply locations, reconcile stale/canceled cell deliveries, and test contention between simultaneous construction plans. Preserve deterministic material custody and existing player-versus-NPC equality. The larger NPC labor/society model remains independent of this bounded logistics milestone.
+
+GitHub remains a source repository and documentation/milestone archive, not a development hub; no remote push was made as part of this local implementation.
